---
title: "Merge queues re-run CI in series"
description: "Everyone's agent works in parallel until the merge, and then the queue takes them one at a time. A queue that re-verifies each integrated candidate in the cloud spends a full CI run per merge, so the line moves at the speed of your slowest job. thwip pins the candidate and merges on evidence that already exists, or on a run done on a developer's own machine. On this repository the lane holds a merge for about fourteen seconds."
